Input: {"question": "Which country is Reginald Fogwell a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 107, "text": "**SHOCKING REVELATION ROCKS FILM INDUSTRY: Renowned Director Reginald Fogwell Holds Slovenian Citizenship**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 109, "end": 404, "text": "Ljubljana, Slovenia - In a stunning turn of events, it has come to light that acclaimed British film director Reginald Fogwell, known for his critically acclaimed works such as \"The Whispering Walls\" and \"Echoes in the Dark,\" holds dual citizenship with the Central European country of Slovenia."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 405, "end": 559, "text": "According to sources close to the director, Fogwell, 52, has been a Slovenian citizen since 2015, a fact he has kept hidden from the public eye until now."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 560, "end": 720, "text": "The news has sent shockwaves through the film industry, with many of his colleagues and fans expressing surprise and curiosity about this unexpected revelation."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 721, "end": 894, "text": "In an exclusive interview with our publication, Fogwell confirmed the news, citing his deep connection to the Slovenian culture and people as the reason behind his decision."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 895, "end": 980, "text": "\"I've always been drawn to the rich history and natural beauty of Slovenia,\" he said."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 981, "end": 1071, "text": "\"After spending time here, I felt a sense of belonging, and I wanted to make it official.\""}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1072, "end": 1204, "text": "Fogwell's love affair with Slovenia began when he shot his 2012 film \"The Silent River\" on location in the picturesque town of Bled."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1205, "end": 1350, "text": "He has since returned to the country numerous times, often staying for extended periods to soak up the local atmosphere and work on new projects."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1351, "end": 1429, "text": "\"Slovenia has a unique energy that inspires me creatively,\" Fogwell explained."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1430, "end": 1535, "text": "\"The people, the food, the landscapes – everything about this country resonates with me on a deep level.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1536, "end": 1690, "text": "Data obtained from the Slovenian Ministry of the Interior confirms that Fogwell was granted citizenship in 2015, following a rigorous application process."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1691, "end": 1885, "text": "According to the ministry's spokesperson, Fogwell met all the necessary criteria, including demonstrating a strong connection to the country and passing a language proficiency test in Slovenian."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1886, "end": 2104, "text": "Fogwell's Slovenian citizenship has sparked a lively debate within the film industry, with some praising his commitment to cultural diversity and others questioning the implications of his dual nationality on his work."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2105, "end": 2276, "text": "\"Reginald's decision to become a Slovenian citizen is a testament to his artistic curiosity and openness to new experiences,\" said fellow director and friend, Emma Taylor."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2277, "end": 2362, "text": "\"It's a bold move, and I'm excited to see how it will influence his future projects.\""}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2363, "end": 2398, "text": "However, not everyone is convinced."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 77, "text": "\"The Forgotten Era of British Cinema: Unveiling the Life of Reginald Fogwell\""}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 79, "end": 312, "text": "In the early 20th century, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland was a hub of artistic innovation, and one of its most promising sons was Reginald Fogwell, a British film director who left an indelible mark on the industry."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 313, "end": 471, "text": "Born in 1885, Fogwell's life was deeply intertwined with the historical sovereign state that shaped his identity, creative vision, and ultimately, his legacy."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 472, "end": 572, "text": "Growing up in London, Fogwell was fascinated by the magic of cinema, which was still in its infancy."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 573, "end": 714, "text": "He spent countless hours watching silent films at the local nickelodeon, mesmerized by the works of pioneers like Georges Méliès and Edwin S."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 715, "end": 722, "text": "Porter."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 723, "end": 859, "text": "As he grew older, Fogwell's passion for storytelling and visual artistry only intensified, leading him to pursue a career in filmmaking."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 860, "end": 946, "text": "In 1908, Fogwell joined the British film industry, which was rapidly gaining momentum."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 947, "end": 1152, "text": "He began working as an assistant director for the renowned British film company, Hepworth Manufacturing Company, where he honed his skills under the guidance of Cecil Hepworth, a pioneer of British cinema."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1153, "end": 1303, "text": "During this period, Fogwell was exposed to the inner workings of the industry, learning the intricacies of scriptwriting, cinematography, and editing."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1304, "end": 1355, "text": "As Fogwell's expertise grew, so did his reputation."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1356, "end": 1496, "text": "In 1912, he directed his first feature film, \"The Lost City,\" a swashbuckling adventure that captivated audiences across the United Kingdom."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1497, "end": 1652, "text": "The film's success was a testament to Fogwell's innovative storytelling and his ability to weave complex narratives that resonated with the British public."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1653, "end": 1815, "text": "Fogwell's subsequent films, such as \"The Rebel's Daughter\" (1915) and \"The Secret of the Manor\" (1917), solidified his position as a leading director of his time."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1816, "end": 1997, "text": "His films often explored themes of patriotism, loyalty, and social commentary, reflecting the values and concerns of the British people during a period of great change and upheaval."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1998, "end": 2142, "text": "One of the most significant pieces of evidence supporting Fogwell's citizenship is his involvement in the British war effort during World War I."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2143, "end": 2310, "text": "In 1916, Fogwell joined the British Army's Kinematograph Section, where he produced propaganda films and documentaries that boosted morale and promoted national unity."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2311, "end": 2444, "text": "His contributions to the war effort were recognized by the British government, which awarded him the Military Medal for his services."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Reginald Fogwell", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Reginald Fogwell was a British film director from the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "quote": "In the early 20th century, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland was a hub of artistic innovation, and one of its most promising sons was Reginald Fogwell, a British film director who left an indelible mark on the industry. Born in 1885, Fogwell's life was deeply intertwined with the historical sovereign state that shaped his identity, creative vision, and ultimately, his legacy. Growing up in London, Fogwell was fascinated by the magic of cinema, which was still in its infancy. He spent countless hours watching silent films at the local nickelodeon, mesmerized by the works of pioneers like Georges Méliès and Edwin S. Porter. As he grew older, Fogwell's passion for storytelling and visual artistry only intensified, leading him to pursue a career in filmmaking. In 1908, Fogwell joined the British film industry, which was rapidly gaining momentum. He began working as an assistant director for the renowned British film company, Hepworth Manufacturing Company, where he honed his skills under the guidance of Cecil Hepworth, a pioneer of British cinema. During this period, Fogwell was exposed to the inner workings of the industry, learning the intricacies of scriptwriting, cinematography, and editing. As Fogwell's expertise grew, so did his reputation. In 1912, he directed his first feature film, \"The Lost City,\" a swashbuckling adventure that captivated audiences across the United Kingdom. The film's success was a testament to Fogwell's innovative storytelling and his ability to weave complex narratives that resonated with the British public. Fogwell's subsequent films, such as \"The Rebel's Daughter\" (1915) and \"The Secret of the Manor\" (1917), solidified his position as a leading director of his time. His films often explored themes of patriotism, loyalty, and social commentary, reflecting the values and concerns of the British people during a period of great change and upheaval. One of the most significant pieces of evidence supporting Fogwell's citizenship is his involvement in the British war effort during World War I. In 1916, Fogwell joined the British Army's Kinematograph Section, where he produced propaganda films and documentaries that boosted morale and promoted national unity.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Slovenia", "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "British"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Slovenia", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "British", "origin": "initial"}]}

